Spec: state

Purpose:
  Own the diagnostic API's `state` item: one instance CRD's full stored object — `metadata`,
    `spec` and a sanitized `status` — rendered as one YAML dump for the `state` endpoint: read
    the requested @TenantInstance, @ServiceInstance or @SystemInstance by kind, blank its
    `tfstate` and `rhaistate` status blobs out of the fetched copy before anything serializes
    them, re-encode the typed object as JSON then YAML, mask the text through @scrub_yaml, and
    hand back the masked text plus its @ScrubStats tally. The dump is the stored-CRD view, not
    Terraform state: the item is named `state` while `tfstate`/`rhaistate` are exactly what this
    file removes; child-object manifests belong to ./children.rs.

Owns:
  ./state.rs

References:
  ../dto.sdd — @ScrubStats is the returned tally; its `X-Diag-Redactions` rendering lives in
    ../server.rs.
  ../error.sdd — the exit lane: only @DiagError::UnknownKind, @DiagError::KubeError,
    @DiagError::SerializationError and @DiagError::YamlError ever leave this file; ids and
    statuses are owned there.
  ../anonymize.sdd — the @scrub_yaml contract: value/regex masking of the text, per-call Secret
    listing over both namespaces, infallibility and counter semantics.
  ../state.sdd — the client arriving as the argument is the @AppState.client handle cloned by
    ../server.rs; the server identity whose RBAC decides the `get` belongs there.
  .../server.rs — sole consumer: pre-validates kind/names, authenticates and authorizes the
    `"state"` item, then renders this dump as the HTTP body.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd, /common/src/instanceservice.sdd,
    /common/src/instancesystem.sdd — the CRD models read and dumped here; their status types are
    what carries the stripped `tfstate`/`rhaistate` fields.

Must:
  Kind dispatch is exact and case-sensitive on the three lowercase plurals `tenantinstances`,
    `serviceinstances`, `systeminstances`; every other @kind string yields
    @DiagError::UnknownKind before this file issues any cluster read.
  Exactly one point read per call: one @Api::namespaced(@client.clone(), `namespace`) plus
    @Api::get of `name` — no `list`, no `watch`, no @ListParams, no selector anywhere in this
    file (the Secret lists happen inside @scrub_yaml, owned by ../anonymize.rs).
  Sanitizing is fixed and in-memory: after the @Ok read and before any serialization, when the
    fetched object carries a `status`, its @status.tfstate and @status.rhaistate become @None —
    all three CRD status types declare both fields; when `status` is @None nothing is mutated;
    no other field is touched, whichever kind was read.
  The dump is the typed serde view with zero rename, filter or reconstruction by this file:
    @serde_json::to_value of the sanitized object, then @serde_yaml::to_string of that tree. Per
    the hand-written @Serialize that @kube-derive `3.1.0` generates, `apiVersion`, `kind`,
    `metadata` and `spec` keys are always emitted in that order and `status` only when @Some;
    because the common status structs declare no @skip_serializing_if, the stripped
    `tfstate`/`rhaistate` keys survive the dump as `null` — the redaction is announced, not
    hidden. Deeper key sets, casing and @metadata rendering belong to the three /common specs.
  Order is frozen: typed read → status strip → @serde_json::to_value → @serde_yaml::to_string →
    @scrub_yaml. Masking therefore consumes the emitted YAML text, never typed fields; the
    instance `namespace` is the first Secret-collection namespace, `vynil_namespace` the second;
    the returned @ScrubStats is that single infallible @scrub_yaml result passed through
    un-aggregated (contrast the saturating per-child fold of ./children.rs).
  Stripped payloads never reach the client or the counters: being removed before serialization,
    tfstate/rhaistate content never enters the JSON tree, the YAML text, the scrubbing pass or
    the redaction counts — a secret stored only there contributes nothing to the text or to
    @ScrubStats.
  Every failure leg aborts the call: there is no degraded-success lane (a child read failure
    degrades in ./children.rs; an instance read failure never does); and the file keeps no
    cache, TTL, informer or global state — every call re-reads.

Must not:
  Write back to the cluster — no patch and no `status`-subresource merge of the kind the
    /common @impl_instance_common! setters perform: stripping `tfstate`/`rhaistate` is a local
    mutation of the fetched copy only, and the stored CRD keeps both payloads untouched by any
    read of this endpoint.

Depends on:
  @kube `3.1.0` (versions locked in /Cargo.lock) — @kube::Client, @kube::@api::@Api; only the
    @namespaced constructor, @get and the cheap @Client @Clone per Api build are used.
  @common — @TenantInstance, @ServiceInstance, @SystemInstance from
    /common/src/instancetenant.rs, /common/src/instanceservice.rs,
    /common/src/instancesystem.rs; read-only consumers here.
  @crate::anonymize::scrub_yaml in ../anonymize.rs — the mask-and-tally step over the rendered
    YAML.
  @crate::dto::@ScrubStats in ../dto.rs — the returned tally type.
  @crate::error::@DiagError in ../error.rs — the exit lane; the three payload variants enter via
    explicit @map_err calls.
  @serde_json::to_value and @serde_yaml::to_string (locked in /Cargo.lock) — the two-hop
    JSON-then-YAML rendering of the dump.

Exposes:
  Full public surface — `pub mod state;` in ./mod.rs under `pub mod collect;` in ../lib.rs — is
    the single function; the file declares no types or constants:
  @get_instance_state — `pub async fn @get_instance_state(client: &@kube::Client, kind: &@str,
    namespace: &@str, name: &@str, vynil_namespace: &@str) -> @Result<(@std::string::@String,
    @ScrubStats), @DiagError>`; its only consumer is ../server.rs, whose `"state"` arm serves
    the text through @yaml_response (`200`, `application/yaml`) and the tally through
    @add_scrub_header (`X-Diag-Redactions`).
  Everything else is private: @get_tenant_instance, @get_service_instance and
    @get_system_instance (`async fn` each, `(&@kube::Client, &@str, &@str) -> @Result<@TenantInstance
    / @ServiceInstance / @SystemInstance, @DiagError>`), same-shape copies differing only in the
    CRD fetched and stripped; their names coincide with the three script-visible Rhai functions
    registered in /common (e.g. `get_tenant_instance` of /common/src/instancetenant.sdd) while
    being module-private and unrelated.

Accepts:
  A live borrowed @kube::Client and four free-form @str borrows, validated nothing here: `kind`
    is re-gated raw against the three plurals (../server.rs checks @VALID_KINDS and DNS forms,
    authenticates and authorizes before calling, but this function independently refuses foreign
    kinds and enforces nothing else); `namespace` serves double duty as the read namespace and
    the first Secret-collection namespace; `name` goes verbatim to @Api::get; `vynil_namespace`
    reaches only @scrub_yaml.
  No precondition on the stored object's shape: it must merely decode into the kind's model — a
    stored CRD that fails that decode surfaces as a @kube::Error through the read leg.

Returns:
  @Ok of `(masked YAML text, @ScrubStats)`. The text is @serde_yaml's rendering of the sanitized
    typed view: `apiVersion: vynil.solidite.fr/v1`, the CRD's `kind`, the full `metadata` the
    API server returned (server-populated `managedFields` and timestamps included — noise is not
    filtered, only values are masked), `spec` verbatim including user-authored `options` and
    `initFrom`, and when present the `status` with every field intact except `tfstate: null` and
    `rhaistate: null`; an absent `status` contributes no `status` key at all. @Ok never carries
    stripped payload content.
  The tally counts @scrub_yaml pass-1 secret replacements over that rendered text only — pattern
    redactions are invisible to the counters per ./anonymize.sdd.

Raises:
  @DiagError::UnknownKind — any `kind` outside the three plurals, raised pre-call with zero
    cluster reads issued.
  @DiagError::KubeError — every @kube::Error from the single instance @get, mapped explicitly by
    @map_err(@DiagError::KubeError): a Kubernetes-side `404` when ../server.rs' existence
    pre-check races a deletion, an RBAC `403`, a model-decode failure — all land in the `500`
    lane; @DiagError::InstanceNotFound is never raised from this file.
  @DiagError::SerializationError — @serde_json::to_value failure, mapped explicitly by
    @map_err.
  @DiagError::YamlError — @serde_yaml::to_string failure, mapped explicitly by @map_err; see
    Tasks for its reachability.
  @scrub_yaml adds no error leg — it is infallible per ./anonymize.sdd; its only failure mode is
    silent under-masking.

Handles:
  Absent `status` — the `if let` @Some strip guard keeps the fetched object untouched and the
    dump loses the whole `status` key; already-@None `tfstate`/`rhaistate` make stripping an
    idempotent no-op while the null keys still render (stripped and never-set stay
    wire-indistinguishable, see Tasks).
  Under-masking inherited from @scrub_yaml — a failed Secret list leaves secret values verbatim
    without failing, and masking stays value/shape-driven only: arbitrary `spec.options` or
    condition `message` content passes through unless it equals a collected Secret value or one
    of the three regex shapes.
  A tenant namespace equal to `vynil_namespace` — one Secret sweep, delegated to
    ../anonymize.rs' equal-namespace rule.

Tasks:
  [ ] No `#[cfg(test)]` module exists in this file and the server crate has no integration tests
      or dev-dependencies today; cover all Scenarios below from these blocks under the project
      TTD rule once a cluster double exists (same constraint recorded in ./children.sdd and
      ./anonymize.sdd).
  [?] @get_instance_state's rustdoc puts the `# Errors` block before its one-line summary, so
      the summary renders inside the errors section — reorder during doc review; its wording
      also claims serialization failures propagate, which Tasks below question.
  [?] The `as per brief §7.4` comments (all three helpers) cite the retired `docs/conception/`
      brief — declared no-authority by `.specdd/bootstrap.project.md` — leaving the strip rule
      with no owning artifact. Decide whether this spec (or /server/server.sdd) becomes that
      authority and drop the stale citation.
  [?] Stripping survives the dump as `tfstate: null` / `rhaistate: null` keys: clients cannot
      distinguish "redacted for you" from "never stored", and the null keys themselves are
      constant noise. Decide later whether the keys are dropped (skip on the common status
      structs), replaced by a placeholder marker, or kept as-is.
  [?] The three helpers are same-shape copies differing only by CRD type and mirror the
      `get_*_children` trio of ./children.rs; decide later whether one generic helper replaces
      all six.
  [?] The @DiagError::SerializationError and @DiagError::YamlError legs are mapped per the doc
      comment yet likely unreachable — serializing an API-decoded typed tree always succeeds, and
      a @serde_json::@Value (string keys, finite numbers) always renders as YAML; the doc comment
      meanwhile claims "serialization of the collected resources" as a live failure. Decide
      whether they propagate (here) or degrade like ./children.rs' @unwrap_or_default lane — and
      reconcile the two crates' stances.
  [?] Secret values whose text gets escaped in serialization (`"`, `\` or newline content emitted
      in a quoted scalar style) may have no literal occurrence in the rendered YAML and so can
      survive @scrub_yaml here — the escape blindness ./anonymize.sdd records for @scrub_json
      applies to this serialized-YAML lane too, contrary to that spec's claim that those secrets
      "still mask in the YAML lane" (that claim holds for raw log text, not for a
      @serde_yaml::to_string product). Decide, together with ./anonymize.sdd, whether the claim,
      the rule set or both get corrected.

Done when:
  Every Scenario below maps to a green test in `server`, the `[?]` decisions above are recorded,
    and `cargo test -p server` with `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and
    `cargo +nightly fmt --check` stays green.

Scenario: The dump is the sanitized CRD view
  Given a @TenantInstance in `tenant-a` whose status holds @Some `tfstate` and @Some `rhaistate`
    and whose `spec.options` carries a collected Secret value
  When @get_instance_state runs with kind `tenantinstances`
  Then exactly one namespaced @Api::get of the instance is issued, and the text carries
    `apiVersion` `vynil.solidite.fr/v1`, `kind` `TenantInstance`, full `metadata` and `spec`,
    while `tfstate` and `rhaistate` render `null` with none of their content anywhere
  And the `options` Secret occurrence becomes `<anonymized>` with @ScrubStats counting that
    pass-1 replacement on the rendered YAML only
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Kind gate refuses pre-call
  Given kind `TenantInstances` with a capital T, or `pods`, or `""`
  When @get_instance_state is awaited
  Then @DiagError::UnknownKind is returned and no cluster request is issued at all
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Deletion race fails as KubeError, never as InstanceNotFound
  Given the instance deleted between ../server.rs' existence pre-check and this file's @get
  When the single read fails with a Kubernetes `404`
  Then the call @Errs @DiagError::KubeError — the `500` lane — because this file distinguishes
    no kube error kind
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Absent status dumps without the status key
  Given a freshly created @SystemInstance whose `status` is @None
  When @get_instance_state runs with kind `systeminstances`
  Then no strip mutation runs, the YAML carries no `status` key at all, and @scrub_yaml still
    masks and counts whatever the remaining text holds
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  Sanitized @TenantInstance dump, skeleton (secrets masked, content elided):
    `apiVersion: vynil.solidite.fr/v1` / `kind: TenantInstance` / `metadata: {name: …, namespace:
    tenant-a, managedFields: […], …}` / `spec: {jukebox: …, category: …, package: …, initFrom:
    null, options: {restic_password: <anonymized>}}` / `status: {conditions: […], tag: …, digest:
    …, tfstate: null, rhaistate: null, befores: […], …}`
  The ../server.rs answer for it: `200`, `Content-Type: application/yaml`, and
    `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct=1;occurrences=1` for exactly the one masked `options` occurrence
    above — tfstate-stored duplicates of that secret value counted nothing.
